  "finalText": "I've fixed the issue the verifier found: T-3112 is now merged into T-3101, so INC-1 covers it.\n\n**Why it belonged in the outage:** T-3112 (\"Deploy jobs failing everywhere\") is an automated build-pipeline alert with company-wide impact, opened at 15:20. It reports that every deploy job is waiting for a runner, which is the same runner outage as T-3101. It had been left as a new ticket with no severity, deadline, assignee or incident link, and my earlier summary missed it.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Merged T-3112 into T-3101,** which stays the survivor because it is the earliest report. Through the merge, T-3112 is now covered by INC-1 and handled at sev1 under T-3101, which meets steps 3 and 4 of the KB-40 runbook.\n- **Kept T-3101's deadline at 2026-03-30 18:52 UTC.** T-3112 had no deadline, so 18:52 is still the earliest one promised on any ticket in the set.\n- **Added a comment on T-3101** recording the merge and why the deadline didn't change.\n\nNothing else from the earlier work changed.",
